.TH AUSCULTE 1 "2026-08-20" "realisateur" "bashified verb"
.SH NAME
ausculte \- can Zach stop looking? Composed from probes that already exist.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ausculte
.br
.B ausculte
--json
.br
.B ausculte
.I probe
.RI [ probe ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs every probe this estate already has and answers one question: is
self-dev healthy enough that a human does not have to keep watching it?
.PP
.B channel
asks whether a question can even reach Zach, through zaxon. It is probed
FIRST and deliberately: every other failure below is meant to reach him
through that same channel, so a green report with the channel down is a
report nobody receives.
.PP
.B hosts
runs
.BR dexter-liveness (1)'s
checks.
.B arming
asks whether the self-dev accounts monkey hosts are armed, resolving the
collector locally when already run from the target host rather than
ssh'ing to itself.
.B propagation
compares the published verb manifest against what is actually installed on
each host.
.B rot
and
.B silence
run
.I decision-rot.sh
and
.BR silence-audit (1)
respectively.
.PP
.B hosts
and
.B rot
call sibling scripts
.RI ( dexter-liveness.sh ", " decision-rot.sh )
that stay repo-only. Run standalone, with no repo clone beside it, those two
probes correctly report BLIND rather than guess \(em BLIND is the honest
answer to "the sibling this probe needs is not here."
.B silence
resolves its sibling three ways (a repo clone's
.IR silence-audit.sh ,
a deployed sibling
.IR silence-audit ,
or PATH), so it keeps working once ausculte ships as a verb.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Print one JSON object per probe instead of the human-readable report.
.TP
.I probe
Run only the named probe(s) instead of every one:
.IR channel ", " hosts ", " arming ", " propagation ", " rot ", " silence .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every declared probe answered OK. Stop looking.
.TP
.B 5
Something declared is DOWN. The report names it.
.TP
.B 6
BLIND: at least one probe could not look, and nothing was found DOWN. This
is NOT "all clear."
.SH NOTES
THE HUMAN CHANNEL IS FIRST, and BLIND is never folded into OK \(em this is
the command built to be believed. Two invariants from its own header have
tests behind them: the channel probe runs before any other, and a BLIND
probe never downgrades to a clean exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR discipline (1),
.BR silence-audit (1)
